;; gap-02 (p58-print-fn): println of a fn. Round 1 refused it (D71: uncatchable
;; `illegal cast`). Since P5.3 (D131) a fn prints in native's shape with the
;; address fixed at 0x0, so a direct println can never match native's
;; `<fn 0x3ce33240a340>`; the program pins the shape through str/pr-str prefixes
;; (not with-out-str: the inlined println ignores *out*, a separate limit). Moved refused -> fixed 2026-10-02.
(println "x")
(println (subs (str (fn [] 1)) 0 6))
(println (subs (pr-str (fn named [] 1)) 0 5))
(println (string? (str (fn [] 1))))
